{"step_index":300,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:51:37Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Yes, I agree. The current interface shows too much information at once. For a beginner, it feels like a developer debugging tool instead of a personal coding teacher.\r\n\r\nMy recommendation: simplify it into a “Teach Me This Code” interface.\r\n\r\nGive your AI coding tool this prompt to modify the existing application.\r\n\r\n1. Simplify the Interface\r\n\r\nRedesign my existing Code Flow Visualizer to make it extremely easy for a complete beginner to understand Python code.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT: Do not rebuild the application from scratch. Modify the existing application and preserve its working execution engine. No AI APIs or external AI services.\r\n\r\n## 1. Simplify the Interface\r\n\r\nRemove the current complicated three-panel developer dashboard, large flowchart, excessive technical labels, and multiple information cards.\r\n\r\nUse a clean, beginner-friendly interface with a light background, large readable text, and minimal distractions.\r\n\r\nThe interface should have only three main areas:\r\n\r\n1. Python code.\r\n\r\n2. Step-by-step explanation.\r\n\r\n3. Variable values.\r\n\r\n## 2. Code Editor\r\n\r\nShow the Python code on the left.\r\n\r\nHighlight only the current line. Keep the remaining code visible but slightly less prominent.\r\n\r\nAdd a simple heading: \"Your Code\".\r\n\r\n## 3. Teaching Area\r\n\r\nMake this the main focus of the screen.\r\n\r\nShow one step at a time using this format:\r\n\r\n**Step 1: Create the variable**\r\n\r\nCode:\r\n`c = 0`\r\n\r\n**What does this mean?**\r\n\r\nWe create a variable named `c` and store the number `0` inside it.\r\n\r\n**Variable values now:**\r\n\r\n`c = 0`\r\n\r\n**What happens next?**\r\n\r\nPython moves to the next line and creates the variable `ans`.\r\n\r\nUse simple English. Explain programming concepts only when needed. Do not overw\n<truncated 14090 bytes>\nde `#iterationPillsBar` so mobile users always see the active line and active iteration pill without manual scrolling.\n   4. **Confirm completion concisely to the user** with clickable file links.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Keep responses concise and formatted in GitHub-style markdown with clickable `[filename](file:///...)` links.\n   - Zero AI APIs; preserve all existing functionality.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 6 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791628786466_88bc671a]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1791628786466_88bc671a.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-10T10:39:48Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791630442219_ffbef1d8]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1791630442219_ffbef1d8.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-10T11:07:22Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791630995276_2331d394]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1791630995276_2331d394.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-10T11:20:28Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791635296816_3e0298d5]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1791635296816_3e0298d5.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-10T12:31:17Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791685829300_6748f239]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/.user_uploaded/media_1791685829300_6748f239.png\nLast Edited: 2026-10-11T02:33:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b